WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:06.300
This is the heavy metal band Zeus,

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:09.060
whose lead singer spent
6 years in a Cuban prison

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:10.270
in the early 90's.

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:11.920
Locked up for having long hair

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.610
and other rock music related offenses.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:15.580
But a decade later,

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:17.160
Zeus joined up with the government

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.790
as part of a new state bureaucracy

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:20.560
called the agency of rock.

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:21.740
Did the band sell out,

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:23.710
or were they making a necessary compromise

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.730
to bring more cultural and
artistic freedom to Cuba?

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:29.140
That's the main question
posed by the new documentary,

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:31.493
Los Ultimos Frikis, out now in VOD.

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:35.780
The film, which was shot
between 2009 and 2019,

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:37.550
charts the rise and fall of Zeus

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:40.360
after a period in which Cuba's
communist government jailed

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:43.510
and tortured musicians,
artists, activists, writers,

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:46.093
and other free-thinking freaks.

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:57.900
Rock music had become a
popular outlet for the angst

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:01.470
and aspirations of young
Cubans starting in the 1970's.

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:02.640
By the 80's, however,

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:05.140
communist government officials
started to crack down

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:07.520
on these anti-authoritarian headbangers,

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:09.210
whose work they branded a dangerous,

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:11.870
ideological diversion from the revolution.

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:13.390
Up through the early 90's,

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:15.470
many rockers continue to be imprisoned,

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:18.410
including Dioni who is the
central character in the film,

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:20.110
but after the fall of the Soviet Union

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:22.780
cutoff Cuba's primary source of revenue.

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:23.830
The country's dictator,

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:26.920
Fidel Castro faced a near
total economic collapse

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.790
and was forced to accept some cultural

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:30.120
and market liberalization

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:32.220
in exchange for foreign investment.

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:35.100
Around that time Dioni
was released from prison

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:37.130
and he proceeded to find even greater fame

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.960
as the lead singer of Zeus,

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:40.380
but as director, Nicholas Brennan,

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:42.400
chronicles in the documentary,

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.590
Cuba's post-Soviet openness to rock

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:46.270
came with strings attached.

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:49.510
The government presented the
band with a Faustian bargain.

00:01:49.510 --> 00:01:52.070
Partner with the newly
created agency of rock,

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:53.140
and in exchange,

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:55.660
Zeus would be able to
perform before huge crowds

00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:57.820
at the only major rock venue in Havana.

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:00.600
Zeus, and I think just
rock and roll in general

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:03.083
was seen historically.

